<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isputahsu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isputahsu was a king of Kizzuwatna in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> around the 15th century BCE and one of the first known rulers of that kingdom. He styled himself <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-king">Great King</a> on his seal. He concluded a treaty with the Hittite king Telipinu, one of the earliest known treaties between equal partners from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">ancient Near East</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isputahsu.jpg" alt="Isputahsu" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gökhan Can Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Luwian_Cultural_Center,_Seal_of_Isputashu_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
